WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.110 --> 00:06.111
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION.

3
00:06.194 --> 00:08.030
THERE IS NO RELATION TO REAL PEOPLE OR EVENTS.

4
00:08.113 --> 00:10.073
[♪ rock music playing]

5
00:41.396 --> 00:44.066
EPISODE 1

6
00:45.817 --> 00:47.653
[tires screech]

7
00:50.572 --> 00:52.282
[♪ funky music plays]

8
00:57.496 --> 01:01.333
Good morning! Hey, Daniel!

9
01:06.046 --> 01:07.047
KARIN'S SWEET POTATO FARM

10
01:08.507 --> 01:11.551
NO OVERTIME - TEMP WORKER FIRST-TIMERS WELCOME

11
01:14.429 --> 01:16.056
-Good morning! -Whoa. [coughs]

12
01:16.139 --> 01:17.474
Hey,

13
01:17.557 --> 01:18.850
-good morning… -I brought you water.

14
01:18.934 --> 01:19.935
Thank you.

15
01:20.018 --> 01:23.689
But, uh, I wish you brought some help instead.

16
01:23.772 --> 01:27.067
I wish I could have brought a hundred people to help.

17
01:27.734 --> 01:31.363
But it's hard to find anyone who wants to do farm work with intensive labor.

18
01:31.446 --> 01:32.823
[sighs]

19
01:35.200 --> 01:38.745
[sighs] That's why the both of us will work extra hard. Okay?

20
01:38.829 --> 01:40.122
[coughs] What?

21
01:41.456 --> 01:42.708
That's too hard!

22
01:42.791 --> 01:46.545
You really expect us to work this entire field ourselves?

23
01:47.921 --> 01:50.257
Really? We can't.

24
01:50.340 --> 01:52.884
It's impossible! [voice echoes]

25
01:52.968 --> 01:54.594
Fine, then. We'll just get

26
01:54.678 --> 01:56.471
-a thousand meters or so done. -What?

27
01:56.555 --> 01:59.766
That's not much. All right. Time's a-ticking. Let's move it.

28
01:59.850 --> 02:01.309
-Come on. -[groans]

29
02:04.563 --> 02:07.732
-[in German] I'm dying out here. -[in English] Huh? What was that?

30
02:07.816 --> 02:09.734
Uh, the sky's nice and clear.

31
02:09.818 --> 02:11.737
[birds squawking]

32
02:11.820 --> 02:13.530
What a nice day!

33
02:15.240 --> 02:17.534
[♪ funky music continues]

34
02:35.510 --> 02:37.262
Good morning.

35
02:37.345 --> 02:40.265
Ah! Good morning, Grandma!

36
02:40.348 --> 02:42.058
[Grandma laughs]

37
02:44.519 --> 02:48.482
[♪ upbeat music playing]

38
03:07.292 --> 03:09.169
[in Korean] The pictures are turning out great here.

39
03:09.252 --> 03:11.296
[friend 1] Yeah? Hey, let's take one together.

40
03:11.379 --> 03:13.590
[friend 2] Sure, let's get someone to take it for us.

41
03:17.093 --> 03:18.595
Would you like me to take it for you?

42
03:19.429 --> 03:20.430
-[friend 2] Oh, would you? -Yeah.

43
03:20.514 --> 03:23.016
Then could you take one of us together? Thank you.

44
03:24.392 --> 03:26.394
Hey, isn't he the CEO of Y:SPACE?

45
03:26.478 --> 03:27.479
Lee Yubin?

46
03:27.562 --> 03:29.314
-[friend 1] Whoa, is that really him? -Yeah!

47
03:29.397 --> 03:32.651
-[friend 1] No way. That's insane. -[friend 2] Wow, how cool! [chuckles]

48
03:36.404 --> 03:38.448
Hey, that came out really pretty.

49
03:38.532 --> 03:40.825
[friend 2] "Pretty"? Thank you.

50
03:40.909 --> 03:43.995
Oh, my gosh, he said we look pretty! Hey, let's see.

51
03:46.039 --> 03:47.040
Huh?

52
03:47.123 --> 03:48.124
What is this?

53
03:48.833 --> 03:50.877
MADE IT TO MONÉA, THE 2025 KME DESIGN AWARD WINNER, AT OPENING!

54
03:50.961 --> 03:52.295
NO WAY, DID YOU SEE LEE YUBIN?

55
03:52.379 --> 03:53.922
YES! HE'S WAY TOO HOT TO BE A SPATIAL DESIGNER

56
04:06.101 --> 04:08.770
We displayed these individually. As for the candles…

57
04:08.853 --> 04:09.896
[gasps]

58
04:09.980 --> 04:11.106
Excuse me for a sec.

59
04:11.189 --> 04:13.066
Boss. Hey, what are you doing here so early?

60
04:13.149 --> 04:15.402
Huh? The opening's not for another two hours.

61
04:17.195 --> 04:19.573
They're from the head office. This is our CEO, Lee Yubin.

62
04:19.656 --> 04:21.616
Why don't you two introduce yourselves and…

63
04:21.700 --> 04:24.578
Wow. Look at you, boss. Working so hard. [chuckles]

64
04:24.661 --> 04:26.329
You're already… What? What is it?

65
04:26.413 --> 04:27.539
[♪ comical music playing]

66
04:27.622 --> 04:29.207
It's a little crooked…

67
04:29.291 --> 04:31.501
Excuse me. Could you make sure these are lined up properly?

68
04:31.585 --> 04:32.627
Yeah.

69
04:32.711 --> 04:34.588
You haven't had your coffee yet, have you?

70
04:34.671 --> 04:36.840
Yeah, let's go grab a nice, hot cup of coffee…

71
04:37.591 --> 04:39.968
Hey, Yubin. Wait, boss. Yubin!

72
04:40.051 --> 04:42.637
-How about some coffee? -Good evening, sir.

73
04:42.721 --> 04:44.890
Come on, have some coffee!

74
04:49.436 --> 04:51.438
-Hey. -Yeah?

75
04:51.521 --> 04:52.522
What…

76
04:54.733 --> 04:55.734
What is that?

77
04:56.735 --> 04:57.736
Wait, you think…

78
04:58.570 --> 05:01.531
You think that color goes with the rest of the space?

79
05:01.615 --> 05:04.159
You really think a red table belongs here?

80
05:05.285 --> 05:08.288
Just let it slide just this once, all right?

81
05:08.371 --> 05:11.875
The client specifically asked for it. They're the one paying--

82
05:11.958 --> 05:16.254
Whoa, boss! How are we supposed to defy the almighty client?

83
05:16.338 --> 05:18.465
That thing's expensive! Please don't.

84
05:19.507 --> 05:21.509
What's the condition in our client contracts?

85
05:23.845 --> 05:27.599
"Lee Yubin's designs are never, ever to be altered."

86
05:30.060 --> 05:32.270
[inhales sharply] Take it away.

87
05:41.780 --> 05:43.239
I learn so much from you every day.

88
05:50.038 --> 05:52.040
SPATIAL DESIGN GRAND PRIZE KOREAN ARCHITECTURE ASSOCIATION

89
05:52.123 --> 05:53.124
SPATIAL DESIGN AWARD - WINNER

90
05:53.208 --> 05:54.209
2023 GARDEN DESIGN AWARD

91
05:54.292 --> 05:55.585
ASSOCIATION OF ARCHITECTS SPECIAL AWARD

92
06:00.882 --> 06:02.050
[sighs]

93
06:02.133 --> 06:03.802
[knocks on door]

94
06:04.511 --> 06:06.888
♪ Want to have a drink with me? ♪

95
06:12.310 --> 06:17.774
Come on, boss. You've got to learn to enjoy yourself once a project's over.

96
06:17.857 --> 06:19.901
This was our first team dinner in six months.

97
06:19.985 --> 06:21.820
You could've shown up.

98
06:21.903 --> 06:24.447
Have you ever seen me at team dinners?

99
06:24.531 --> 06:26.992
All a CEO needs to do is keep his mouth shut and pick up the bill.

100
06:27.075 --> 06:28.326
Why make everyone uncomfortable?

101
06:28.410 --> 06:29.577
You're so uptight.

102
06:30.203 --> 06:32.580
[sighs] Ease up a little, will you?

103
06:32.664 --> 06:34.541
That way, the staff might actually follow you…

104
06:34.624 --> 06:35.667
Ease up?

105
06:37.127 --> 06:38.169
Hey.

106
06:39.462 --> 06:42.757
We put our company's reputation on the line to win this project.

107
06:42.841 --> 06:45.301
All right? And we beat 100-to-1 odds to get it, no less.

108
06:45.385 --> 06:46.845
Giving it all might still fall short.

109
06:46.928 --> 06:48.847
-But you want me to ease up? -All right.

110
06:48.930 --> 06:50.140
Yeah, you're right.

111
06:50.223 --> 06:54.269
Once this project's finished, your name's going global.

112
06:54.352 --> 06:55.687
I know that.

113
06:57.605 --> 06:58.606
Here you go.

114
06:59.649 --> 07:00.692
Cheers.

115
07:06.156 --> 07:10.493
Now that the investors are finally done with their review,

116
07:10.577 --> 07:12.162
looks like all that's left is for us to sign!

117
07:12.245 --> 07:13.705
Hey, but this…

118
07:15.707 --> 07:17.500
Are you sure this is legit?

119
07:17.584 --> 07:20.587
-Huh? -I mean, this is a huge project,

120
07:21.296 --> 07:23.882
and they're investing in a startup like us?

121
07:25.049 --> 07:27.093
-Does that even make sense? -Lee Yubin.

122
07:28.845 --> 07:31.055
You, our CEO. That's who they believe in.

123
07:32.015 --> 07:34.017
The legal review's totally clear. Everything checks out.

124
07:36.811 --> 07:38.563
-Good work. -[chuckles]

125
07:38.646 --> 07:42.817
Oh, the contract. Here, you should look it over too.

126
07:43.651 --> 07:45.695
It's fine. I'm sure you've handled it just fine.

127
07:46.613 --> 07:47.614
Nah, come on.

128
07:47.697 --> 07:49.365
I'm busy, man. You take care of it.

129
07:51.201 --> 07:52.202
All right.

130
07:52.911 --> 07:57.749
Don't worry about this kind of thing. You just focus on the design work, okay?

131
07:57.832 --> 08:00.668
I'll take care of all the tedious stuff like this.

132
08:00.752 --> 08:02.629
Oh, and this.

133
08:03.838 --> 08:06.007
-Well, it was on my desk. -What is it?

134
08:06.090 --> 08:07.759
I think the newbie got confused.

135
08:07.842 --> 08:09.844
What's this? Japan?

136
08:12.180 --> 08:16.601
Oh, sorry. I thought it was for me and opened it.

137
08:17.519 --> 08:21.606
Hey, looks like your father left you some land in Japan.

138
08:25.485 --> 08:27.028
INFORMATION REGARDING YOUR UNSETTLED INHERITANCE

139
08:27.111 --> 08:28.112
[Yubin] You speak Japanese?

140
08:28.863 --> 08:31.991
Well, Japan is a major market for us.

141
08:32.742 --> 08:34.536
I had a quick look, and it's an island.

142
08:34.619 --> 08:38.748
Imagine turning that island into a resort.

143
08:39.290 --> 08:40.291
Huh?

144
08:41.501 --> 08:43.336
Hey, take a closer look.

145
08:43.419 --> 08:45.380
-Director Kim. -Yeah?

146
08:45.463 --> 08:48.216
What, should we start another meeting now?

147
08:50.009 --> 08:53.096
Wait… Start another meeting with you? No, I'd rather…

148
08:54.097 --> 08:56.057
[gulps, groans]

149
08:57.976 --> 08:59.227
Oh, boy.

150
09:00.353 --> 09:01.563
Bongsu.

151
09:02.063 --> 09:03.231
Bongsu!

152
09:05.066 --> 09:06.276
[in English] Good night.

153
09:09.863 --> 09:10.989
[in Korean] Geez.

154
09:21.749 --> 09:24.919
NOTICE REGARDING THE SALE OF LAND

155
09:25.003 --> 09:30.967
FARMLAND IN JAPAN REGISTERED UNDER THE LATE LEE GYEONGSU…

156
09:31.050 --> 09:32.886
What is this? "Land sale"?

157
09:34.387 --> 09:35.388
"Charo Island"?

158
09:38.683 --> 09:39.976
KARIN'S STRAWBERRIES

159
09:40.059 --> 09:42.937
[Karin, in English] Good morning. Long time no see.

160
09:43.021 --> 09:44.606
-How are things? -Good morning.

161
09:44.689 --> 09:46.524
Nice sweet potato harvest this year.

162
09:46.608 --> 09:49.569
Yes, good morning! Mrs. Osono.

163
09:49.652 --> 09:51.404
Freshly-harvested sweet potatoes.

164
09:51.487 --> 09:53.740
Oh, Karin! Good morning!

165
09:53.823 --> 09:56.075
Good morning. Here's a free sample just for you.

166
09:56.159 --> 09:58.286
Your berries are ripe already?

167
09:58.369 --> 10:01.122
And we're introducing a new variety next year.

168
10:01.206 --> 10:04.334
When we do, please put them front and center.

169
10:04.417 --> 10:06.961
You're certainly very skilled.

170
10:07.045 --> 10:09.214
I hope that everything goes well for you this season.

171
10:09.297 --> 10:13.009
You know I'll bring you the best ones. Be on the lookout, all right?

172
10:13.593 --> 10:16.304
[shop owner] I've heard that one a few too many times.

173
10:17.347 --> 10:20.850
Why bother with this variety? Doesn't even flower.

174
10:25.104 --> 10:26.105
[Karin sighs]

175
10:28.900 --> 10:33.363
With our strawberries, we ensure that Mother Nature ripens them naturally.

176
10:33.446 --> 10:36.491
They're more delicious than any strawberry you've tasted.

177
10:38.618 --> 10:41.704
Even if they take time more and effort, that's precisely why

178
10:41.788 --> 10:43.206
ours are the best ones.

179
10:43.957 --> 10:45.959
Oh, someone is cocky about her berries, huh?

180
10:46.042 --> 10:47.460
You wanna bet on it?

181
10:49.337 --> 10:51.839
Uh… I've got deliveries to run.

182
10:54.801 --> 10:58.596
You're as strong-willed as ever, dear. [laughs]

183
10:58.680 --> 11:01.808
Hey, once my strawberries have been officially certified,

184
11:01.891 --> 11:05.144
then it's gonna be all over for everybody else.

185
11:08.564 --> 11:10.483
[screams, in Korean] No! I'm not doing this!

186
11:10.566 --> 11:12.610
-Hey, wait! -Let go of me.

187
11:12.694 --> 11:14.487
What matters here is the model, okay?

188
11:14.570 --> 11:16.155
Hey. Dang it!

189
11:16.948 --> 11:18.408
Why's my hair looking like this?

190
11:18.491 --> 11:20.702
And what's with that giant fan?

191
11:20.785 --> 11:21.828
Huh?

192
11:21.911 --> 11:24.122
-[fan whirring] -[director] Hey, hey!

193
11:24.205 --> 11:26.457
Cut, cut.

194
11:26.541 --> 11:27.959
Oh, shoot, this is…

195
11:28.042 --> 11:29.294
My hair…

196
11:29.877 --> 11:31.587
Shoot.

197
11:36.259 --> 11:37.719
-Oh, boy. -[huffs]

198
11:40.763 --> 11:45.059
Hey, don't look at things like that. "Y:SPACE is taking the world by storm."

199
11:45.560 --> 11:46.561
[blows]

200
11:47.061 --> 11:49.355
Look, we don't need any models or celebrities.

201
11:49.439 --> 11:52.066
We need an ad with your face on it

202
11:52.150 --> 11:53.901
to attract investors more easily.

203
11:53.985 --> 11:55.987
How many times do I have to tell you, boss?

204
11:56.070 --> 11:59.449
-Don't you… Ow. Don't you trust me? -I'm not doing it.

205
11:59.532 --> 12:01.117
[huffs] Come on.

206
12:01.200 --> 12:04.662
Hey, you're the CEO. The face of this company!

207
12:04.746 --> 12:06.831
Our star! Okay?

208
12:07.540 --> 12:08.583
Not happening.

209
12:09.625 --> 12:10.918
Swedish furniture.

210
12:12.295 --> 12:14.505
[Yubin whines] Swedish furniture…

211
12:14.589 --> 12:17.175
If this goes well, you might finally get to collaborate

212
12:17.258 --> 12:20.928
with that Swedish luxury furniture brand you were talking about, you know.

213
12:21.012 --> 12:23.014
And if we go into next month's meeting with this ad,

214
12:23.097 --> 12:24.682
we'll make a better impression.

215
12:27.060 --> 12:28.102
I get it.

216
12:28.728 --> 12:29.937
This is new to you.

217
12:30.605 --> 12:31.981
You're uncomfortable.

218
12:32.065 --> 12:35.693
But just bite the bullet and think, "This is for the future of our company,"

219
12:36.444 --> 12:37.945
and give it a go.

220
12:38.029 --> 12:40.573
They said once they touch it all up with CGI, it'll look amazing.

221
12:40.656 --> 12:42.533
[crew member] All right, Yubin. Please stand by.

222
12:42.617 --> 12:44.160
Oh, yeah, he's coming!

223
12:44.243 --> 12:48.748
The gorgeous superstar Lee Yubin is on his way! He's coming!

224
12:48.831 --> 12:50.750
[chuckles] Yep, he's on his way.

225
12:50.833 --> 12:53.503
[♪ opera music playing]

226
13:04.597 --> 13:08.059
[Yubin] Where every moment you stay comes alive.

227
13:08.726 --> 13:11.896
Y:SPACE is taking the world by storm.

228
13:13.439 --> 13:14.774
A space made just for you…

229
13:14.857 --> 13:16.609
[grunts] Shoot.

230
13:16.692 --> 13:17.693
Y:SPACE.

231
13:18.444 --> 13:21.906
Smile, Yubin! Smile!

232
13:24.909 --> 13:25.910
Dang it!

233
13:25.993 --> 13:27.578
THE TWO FACES OF A STAR SPATIAL DESIGNER

234
13:27.662 --> 13:28.663
Y:SPACE IS DONE FOR

235
13:28.746 --> 13:30.498
THE POPULAR PLANNER, JUST A FIGUREHEAD ALL ALONG

236
13:30.581 --> 13:31.624
WAS HE A CON ARTIST ALL ALONG?!

237
13:31.707 --> 13:33.584
[♪ rock music playing]

238
13:33.668 --> 13:36.796
[reporter] Lee Yubin, an internationally award-winning spatial designer,

239
13:36.879 --> 13:38.923
has recently become embroiled in fraud allegations

240
13:39.006 --> 13:41.259
related to an urban redevelopment project.

241
13:41.342 --> 13:42.593
RECENTS KIM BONGSU

242
13:44.428 --> 13:47.473
[automated voice] The number you have dialed is not in service.

243
13:47.557 --> 13:49.851
Please check the number and try again.

244
13:51.477 --> 13:52.895
Kim Bongsu!

245
13:52.979 --> 13:55.189
How can we tell you anything when nothing's confirmed?

246
13:55.273 --> 13:57.316
No, it's not like that. Please just leave your number.

247
13:57.400 --> 14:03.322
-But we're not… -We cannot speak on this matter.

248
14:03.406 --> 14:05.616
It's a surprise to us too. So how can we tell you anything?

249
14:05.700 --> 14:07.160
Apparently, Director Kim took everything and ran.

250
14:07.243 --> 14:09.036
Weren't the two of them supposed to be best friends?

251
14:09.120 --> 14:10.788
[employee] Exactly.

252
14:11.414 --> 14:12.498
What's Mr. Lee going to do?

253
14:12.582 --> 14:15.459
He was betrayed by his friend, and now he's taking the fall. Geez.

254
14:15.543 --> 14:18.671
Well, what's going to happen to our paychecks?

255
14:20.756 --> 14:22.091
[door slams open]

256
14:22.175 --> 14:23.801
-Where's Lee Yubin? -What's going on?

257
14:23.885 --> 14:25.136
[clamoring]

258
14:25.219 --> 14:28.723
[reporter] It was later revealed that Kim, a registered director and business partner

259
14:28.806 --> 14:31.976
at Lee's company, Y:SPACE, collected the project's advance payments

260
14:32.059 --> 14:33.644
in multiple installments before disappearing.

261
14:33.728 --> 14:35.354
Although Lee maintains that he was not involved

262
14:35.438 --> 14:37.023
in the business side of the project,

263
14:37.106 --> 14:40.067
it won't be easy for him to escape legal and moral responsibility.

264
14:40.151 --> 14:41.986
This is Kwon Gunam, IMP News.

265
14:42.069 --> 14:43.654
[people clamoring]

266
14:45.740 --> 14:48.159
Huh? What the… What's going on?

267
14:50.119 --> 14:51.454
Where's my paycheck?

268
15:02.423 --> 15:03.424
NOTICE OF BUSINESS CLOSURE

269
15:03.507 --> 15:05.509
WE THANK EVERYONE WHO HAS SUPPORTED OUR COMPANY

270
15:05.593 --> 15:06.802
WE APOLOGIZE FOR THIS ANNOUNCEMENT

271
15:06.886 --> 15:08.429
AND ARE GRATEFUL FOR THE SUPPORT YOU HAVE SHOWN US

272
15:08.512 --> 15:09.513
LEE YUBIN CEO OF Y:SPACE INC.

273
15:23.653 --> 15:25.488
FOR RENT

274
15:25.571 --> 15:27.615
[engine starts]

275
15:35.039 --> 15:36.290
Geez.

276
15:38.459 --> 15:40.044
[coughs]

277
15:45.675 --> 15:46.884
-[friend] Geez. -[Yubin groans]

278
15:47.677 --> 15:49.720
-What? Come on. -Kim Bongsu, that jerk.

279
15:49.804 --> 15:52.306
I knew something was off. You can tell a lot from a person's face.

280
15:52.390 --> 15:55.977
[Yubin] Couldn't you have come in a little later? It's too early.

281
15:56.060 --> 15:58.354
-Geez. -Hey, it's broad daylight. Get up.

282
15:58.437 --> 16:00.398
How can you be so relaxed?

283
16:00.481 --> 16:01.691
You sold your place with no backup plan.

284
16:01.774 --> 16:02.775
TAX ACCOUNTANT CHOI HYEJIN

285
16:02.858 --> 16:04.652
-What are you going to do now? -I don't know, okay? I don't!

286
16:04.735 --> 16:07.655
I don't know. Everyone was up in arms, demanding their money back.

287
16:07.738 --> 16:09.865
-What choice did I have? -Hold on.

288
16:09.949 --> 16:12.285
What's with those pajamas? Don't tell me they're designer.

289
16:12.368 --> 16:13.995
Why didn't you sell those?

290
16:14.078 --> 16:15.871
How could I sell these? They're my dignity.

291
16:15.955 --> 16:17.039
Would you sell your dignity?

292
16:17.123 --> 16:20.167
Maybe it'll take sleeping on the street to knock some sense into you.

293
16:20.251 --> 16:21.752
[Yubin groans] Dang it.

294
16:22.461 --> 16:25.423
[sighs] Whatever.

295
16:25.506 --> 16:28.718
Anyway, the urgent stuff's mostly taken care of.

296
16:28.801 --> 16:31.679
I scraped together enough to pay all the employees' severance too.

297
16:31.762 --> 16:35.433
I'm completely broke now.

298
16:36.851 --> 16:38.644
Well, not completely.

299
16:40.938 --> 16:42.064
What?

300
16:42.148 --> 16:44.317
Looks like you still have some inherited assets.

301
16:44.400 --> 16:45.401
Huh? Assets?

302
16:45.484 --> 16:47.403
A piece of land in Japan under your father's name.

303
16:48.904 --> 16:52.491
NOTICE REGARDING SALE OF LAND

304
16:53.117 --> 16:54.618
Ah! Ah! Ah!

305
16:54.702 --> 16:57.538
Right! Oh, yeah.

306
16:57.621 --> 16:59.457
Oh, the land. I've got land.

307
16:59.540 --> 17:02.752
Since it's overseas property, it's a bit complicated.

308
17:02.835 --> 17:03.836
Okay.

309
17:03.919 --> 17:07.631
But it's a pretty sizeable piece of land, so if you sell it at a good price…

310
17:08.799 --> 17:10.968
Hey, okay. Hang on.

311
17:11.052 --> 17:12.762
So what do I do from here?

312
17:16.015 --> 17:18.726
AKATSUKI CITY GREEN NOVA CORPORATION

313
17:20.519 --> 17:23.564
[in English] Now I'll need the documents on your crop variety…

314
17:23.647 --> 17:26.901
I marked it with a red sticky note. Ah! I found it. Here it is.

315
17:26.984 --> 17:29.654
Thank you. It's my first year here. I'm sorry it's taking a while.

316
17:29.737 --> 17:31.447
Don't worry. You can take your time.

317
17:33.491 --> 17:35.201
-This is it? -Uh-huh.

318
17:35.284 --> 17:37.995
That's all the relevant documents we need from you.

319
17:39.538 --> 17:41.707
As for the next step…

320
17:41.791 --> 17:42.792
Crop inspection.

321
17:42.875 --> 17:45.628
Yes, that's right. You're an expert at this.

322
17:46.462 --> 17:49.048
Well, this is my third year coming here,

323
17:49.131 --> 17:52.385
and my third year attempt at passing this.

324
17:54.261 --> 17:57.223
Uh, you seem thoroughly prepared.

325
17:57.306 --> 17:59.141
That's why I'm sure that you'll succeed.

326
17:59.725 --> 18:01.310
Thank you very much.

327
18:01.394 --> 18:04.730
I've heard that three years in a row now, but I appreciate it.

328
18:05.690 --> 18:07.483
I'm terribly sorry.

329
18:07.566 --> 18:09.610
[chuckles] It's no big deal.

330
18:09.694 --> 18:12.655
For some reason, I have a really good feeling this year.

331
18:12.738 --> 18:15.032
-[laughs] -Oh, that's good.

332
18:15.116 --> 18:17.702
So it's a decent size, and the pH of the soil is stable.

333
18:17.785 --> 18:20.162
I told you. The strawberries are very good.

334
18:20.246 --> 18:23.040
They're tart, high in natural sugar, and have the best aroma…

335
18:23.124 --> 18:25.918
Oh, I'd say you're not quite out of the woods yet.

336
18:26.001 --> 18:28.087
I didn't see you standing there.

337
18:28.170 --> 18:30.381
You nearly scared me half to death, sir.

338
18:30.464 --> 18:33.843
Paperwork is easy. It's the crop inspection that really gets you.

339
18:33.926 --> 18:36.220
-You know that? -I'm well aware and prepared.

340
18:36.303 --> 18:39.473
I've seen my grandfather go through this process again and again.

341
18:39.557 --> 18:42.435
Quiz. Tagawa, off the top of your head,

342
18:42.518 --> 18:46.188
tell me what it takes to pass crop inspection. Let's hear it, kid.

343
18:47.565 --> 18:51.235
Over 80% of the field, uh, must bear fruit.

344
18:51.318 --> 18:54.613
Also, the consistency of the fruit's size,

345
18:54.697 --> 18:57.032
its firmness and sweetness,

346
18:57.116 --> 18:59.493
must match what's listed in the submitted paperwork.

347
18:59.577 --> 19:01.746
Oh. There you have it.

348
19:01.829 --> 19:03.831
-[sigh] -[Karin chuckles]

349
19:03.914 --> 19:05.750
Well, feel free to stop by anytime.

350
19:05.833 --> 19:07.877
I'll show you the best strawberries you'll ever taste.

351
19:07.960 --> 19:09.795
[laughs]

352
19:09.879 --> 19:11.547
I'd be happy to come by.

353
19:11.630 --> 19:15.593
You're going to surpass your grandfather as a farmer if you keep going like that.

354
19:17.344 --> 19:20.097
So I'll see you in three days for the crop inspection.

355
19:20.181 --> 19:22.767
Great. I'm looking forward to it.

356
19:22.850 --> 19:25.102
Oh! I'm gonna miss the ferry! See you later.

357
19:25.186 --> 19:26.896
-Thank you as always! -Have a nice ride back.

358
19:26.979 --> 19:28.147
Bye!

359
19:29.523 --> 19:31.942
[ferry horn blows]

360
19:33.819 --> 19:34.904
FUKUOKA PIER - FERRY TERMINAL 1

361
19:34.987 --> 19:36.280
[Yubin] Thank you.

362
19:38.657 --> 19:43.454
[in Korean] Hey, they only run three ferries a day to the island.

363
19:43.537 --> 19:45.039
How tiny is this place?

364
19:45.122 --> 19:47.374
[Hyejin] You got all the paperwork ready, right?

365
19:47.458 --> 19:51.003
Yeah. I'll just take one last look around and head straight back.

366
19:51.086 --> 19:53.714
Why? Since you're there, why not stay and relax for a bit?

367
19:53.798 --> 19:58.052
Hey, are you kidding me? What's there to do on that tiny little island?

368
19:58.135 --> 20:00.346
[announcer, in English] Dear passengers, the ferry bound for Charo Island…

369
20:00.429 --> 20:03.307
-[in Korean] I think it's here. Gotta go. -[in English] …will disembark momentarily.

370
20:03.390 --> 20:05.893
If you have not boarded the ferry yet please gather…

371
20:05.976 --> 20:07.978
-Charo Island, please. -Charo Island.

372
20:08.062 --> 20:09.688
Oh. [chuckles]

373
20:11.565 --> 20:13.234
This is the last ticket.

374
20:13.317 --> 20:14.485
-What? -Huh?

375
20:14.568 --> 20:17.154
[Yubin, in Korean] Is he saying there's only one ticket left?

376
20:17.238 --> 20:20.282
[in English] Uh, do you mind if I buy the last ticket?

377
20:20.866 --> 20:23.619
[in Korean] Sorry? No, I mean… What's she saying?

378
20:24.286 --> 20:26.330
[in English] I-- I'm Korean.

379
20:26.413 --> 20:29.667
-I'm sorry. -Oh. You're Korean… [stammers]

380
20:31.293 --> 20:34.797
[clears throat] I'm in a hurry. Could you let me buy the ticket?

381
20:39.093 --> 20:42.680
[in Korean] I'm really sorry, but I've got something important too. I'm sorry.

382
20:46.767 --> 20:48.269
[groaning]

383
20:49.770 --> 20:52.106
[in English] I'm not feeling so great. Could I…

384
20:52.189 --> 20:54.608
[in Korean] What? You were sprinting just fine a second ago.

385
20:56.777 --> 20:58.028
[Karin clears throat]

386
20:59.071 --> 21:00.781
[in English] Well, I was here first, before you.

387
21:00.865 --> 21:02.992
[in Korean] But I touched the counter first.

388
21:03.576 --> 21:04.577
[sighs]

389
21:09.081 --> 21:10.916
[automated voice, in English] Rock, scissors, paper.

390
21:12.626 --> 21:14.086
-Huh? -Rock, scissors, paper…

391
21:14.169 --> 21:15.880
[in Korean] Rock… Rock, paper, scissors?

392
21:15.963 --> 21:17.506
-Hurry up. -No, come on.

393
21:17.590 --> 21:20.342
We're not actually doing rock, paper, scissors for a ticket, are we?

394
21:20.426 --> 21:21.635
[in English] Give up?

395
21:22.136 --> 21:23.220
"Give up"?

396
21:23.304 --> 21:25.848
-[in Korean] Rock, paper, scissors! -[in English] Hey, I wasn't ready.

397
21:33.480 --> 21:36.901
[Yubin thinking, in Korean] Welcome to the ruthless world of competition.

398
21:58.923 --> 22:00.341
[in English] Ready, go.

399
22:00.424 --> 22:01.425
Ready, go.

400
22:07.890 --> 22:12.311
[in Korean] Ugh! I should've thrown rock! I should've…

401
22:12.394 --> 22:15.773
Hey, listen. In Korea, we do best two out of three. One more round, please.

402
22:15.856 --> 22:19.068
[in English] Welcome to the cutthroat world of competition, sir.

403
22:23.155 --> 22:24.198
EXIT

404
22:24.823 --> 22:26.325
Oh, it's Daniel!

405
22:26.408 --> 22:28.118
Daniel! Daniel!

406
22:29.203 --> 22:31.205
Daniel! Hang on.

407
22:31.288 --> 22:32.957
You can't leave yet!

408
22:35.000 --> 22:37.795
I'm sorry. I can't stay any longer.

409
22:39.254 --> 22:42.383
No, Daniel, you can't go. I need you to stay here.

410
22:42.466 --> 22:43.968
-I can't do it by myself. -Not my problem.

411
22:44.802 --> 22:46.971
-Daniel, please… -Let go!

412
22:47.054 --> 22:49.306
You have to stay! I need you!

413
22:49.390 --> 22:52.226
You're the strongest man I've ever met in my entire life!

414
22:52.309 --> 22:53.769
What?

415
22:53.852 --> 22:55.187
[in Korean] What is she doing?

416
22:55.270 --> 22:58.732
[in English] You beg me every day to go harder and put my muscle into it.

417
22:58.816 --> 23:01.235
I don't have the stamina to do what you want.

418
23:02.027 --> 23:05.072
-Please, don't leave me. -[in Korean] Wow, she's intense.

419
23:05.155 --> 23:07.700
[Karin, in English] Is it money? I'll give you so much money…

420
23:07.783 --> 23:08.867
How much do you want?

421
23:08.951 --> 23:10.244
I don't want anything.

422
23:10.327 --> 23:13.497
-Give it to me. -Please. Think this over.

423
23:13.580 --> 23:16.166
Don't be rash. Stay. I need you. Stay!

424
23:16.250 --> 23:17.876
[grunts] Stay!

425
23:25.259 --> 23:26.760
You cheated!

426
23:26.844 --> 23:28.178
-Daniel, please! -Let me go!

427
23:28.971 --> 23:31.181
[Karin] Don't leave!

428
23:33.684 --> 23:35.853
"Could I have a copy of the plat map?"

429
23:35.936 --> 23:37.229
Could I have a copy of…

430
23:37.312 --> 23:38.731
COULD I HAVE A COPY OF THE PLAT MAP?

431
23:38.814 --> 23:40.607
"Could I have a copy of the plat map?"

432
23:43.444 --> 23:44.820
"Could I…"

433
23:44.903 --> 23:46.030
Oh, uh…

434
23:56.623 --> 23:58.375
[♪ pop music playing on radio]

435
24:01.336 --> 24:02.963
[in Korean] I don't even like these anymore.

436
24:05.257 --> 24:07.134
Just one a day, okay?

437
24:07.217 --> 24:10.596
Don't eat like a dozen and get an earful from your mom again like last time.

438
24:11.263 --> 24:14.099
Have you been guarding her well while I was away?

439
24:14.183 --> 24:15.517
Guarding her?

440
24:16.977 --> 24:18.353
What am I, a dog?

441
24:20.147 --> 24:21.899
Hey, are you already going through puberty?

442
24:25.694 --> 24:28.447
You'll be working here in Korea for a while, right?

443
24:38.540 --> 24:40.334
I've got to go back in a week.

444
24:40.417 --> 24:41.877
And this time, I'll be away a bit longer.

445
24:44.797 --> 24:46.006
Why don't you just move there?

446
25:01.021 --> 25:02.981
They still make these, huh?

447
25:03.065 --> 25:04.942
[in English] Where did my candy go?

448
25:05.526 --> 25:06.860
Under here?

449
25:06.944 --> 25:07.986
It's not there.

450
25:08.070 --> 25:09.404
[in Korean] Looking for this?

451
25:10.823 --> 25:13.242
[in English] Thank you very much.

452
25:13.325 --> 25:15.702
Thank you very much. [chuckles]

453
25:22.960 --> 25:24.086
[sighs]

454
25:26.171 --> 25:28.090
[in Korean] I'll just sell it off and be done with it.

455
25:28.674 --> 25:30.050
Should be simple enough.

456
25:32.094 --> 25:34.054
[in English] It's not that easy.

457
25:34.638 --> 25:37.474
Please, sir. Can you really not find anyone?

458
25:37.558 --> 25:40.519
I asked around, but no one's available.

459
25:40.602 --> 25:43.021
No one who wants to work on your farm, anyway.

460
25:43.105 --> 25:44.106
Huh? Why not?

461
25:44.189 --> 25:47.818
The work is physically demanding, there's nothing to do on the island,

462
25:47.901 --> 25:50.571
and they're all terrified of the owner.

463
25:50.654 --> 25:52.823
What? They think that I'm--

464
25:52.906 --> 25:55.325
Oh, whatever. I'm nice. I'm not terrifying at all.

465
25:56.118 --> 26:00.122
Listen, Karin, what if you call it quits? Do something easier?

466
26:00.789 --> 26:02.958
Somebody your size isn't made for farm work.

467
26:03.041 --> 26:04.835
[sighs] You listen.

468
26:04.918 --> 26:06.795
I've worked five years on my own

469
26:06.879 --> 26:09.173
and ten with my grandfather before that.

470
26:10.090 --> 26:15.137
On top of that, if your strawberries don't get certified this time,

471
26:15.220 --> 26:17.431
your relief aid will get pulled.

472
26:17.514 --> 26:18.557
Aren't you worried?

473
26:18.640 --> 26:21.518
Yes, of course I am, and that's why this whole thing matters!

474
26:21.602 --> 26:23.103
You know that as well as I do.

475
26:23.187 --> 26:24.605
Karin, calm down.

476
26:28.442 --> 26:29.860
Even so…

477
26:31.486 --> 26:34.406
finding any new employees around here,

478
26:34.489 --> 26:36.700
it's certainly not easy.

479
26:39.244 --> 26:40.495
Ah…

480
26:41.955 --> 26:42.956
Hmm?

481
26:43.874 --> 26:45.876
Karin, what have you got there?

482
26:49.254 --> 26:50.380
Where'd you get that?

483
26:50.964 --> 26:52.883
It's a really expensive bottle.

484
26:52.966 --> 26:55.928
I know. It's your favorite, right?

485
26:56.011 --> 26:57.971
[both chuckle]

486
26:59.223 --> 27:00.641
Whoa!

487
27:01.934 --> 27:03.810
Mmm, mmm! [chuckles]

488
27:04.394 --> 27:06.146
Oh! Oh.

489
27:06.230 --> 27:08.982
So, you sure you can't find anyone?

490
27:09.900 --> 27:13.946
Well… what sort of employee are you looking for?

491
27:14.446 --> 27:16.740
I'll make sure to find you the right fit.

492
27:20.077 --> 27:21.787
[child] He's throwing up!

493
27:21.870 --> 27:24.164
[people exclaiming]

494
27:24.247 --> 27:26.249
Firstly, they need to be strong…

495
27:26.333 --> 27:27.918
[retching]

496
27:28.001 --> 27:29.503
[children exclaiming]

497
27:32.464 --> 27:33.465
[in Korean] What…

498
27:34.466 --> 27:36.760
Come on, how come I can't get a signal?

499
27:37.552 --> 27:39.388
Come on, give me a signal already.

500
27:39.471 --> 27:41.014
Geez! Why won't it connect?

501
27:43.183 --> 27:45.727
-[in English] …a pleasant personality… -Right.

502
27:46.645 --> 27:48.522
But as for looks…

503
27:54.653 --> 27:56.279
Anything works. Doesn't matter.

504
27:57.531 --> 28:00.450
Oh! Hello!

505
28:04.621 --> 28:06.748
CHARO ISLAND VILLAGE BUS HAMANOKUCHI - IRIE

506
28:06.832 --> 28:08.542
NEXT IS SHIOHAMA

507
28:18.677 --> 28:21.805
-The next bus isn't coming for a while. -Hey?

508
28:21.888 --> 28:24.224
They only run three a day. You just missed one.

509
28:25.350 --> 28:28.770
Look. See? No buses. Where you heading?

510
28:28.854 --> 28:30.397
I can give you a ride. Just hop in.

511
28:31.064 --> 28:32.065
Come on.

512
28:34.359 --> 28:35.944
I don't have all day here.

513
28:36.028 --> 28:37.195
[groans]

514
28:37.279 --> 28:39.823
-Hurry up, would you? -[in Korean] Wait, no more buses.

515
28:39.906 --> 28:42.409
[in English] I said I'd take you. Get in the car.

516
28:42.492 --> 28:45.037
[groans] I'm okay, thank you.

517
28:45.120 --> 28:47.122
-Get in here. Come on. -I… Okay.

518
28:47.789 --> 28:48.957
-Hop in. -I'm okay.

519
28:53.503 --> 28:56.882
-And now it's pouring. [sighs] -[Yubin exclaims]

520
28:56.965 --> 28:58.050
[screams]

521
28:58.133 --> 28:59.760
[in Korean] I'll take that ride! I'll take it!

522
28:59.843 --> 29:01.511
-[in English] Help. Help me, help me. -Buckle up.

523
29:01.595 --> 29:03.221
Help me, help me.

524
29:25.327 --> 29:29.539
[in Korean] Shoot… This weather… It's going to be okay, right?

525
29:34.336 --> 29:36.797
[in English] What are you gonna do over at the village office?

526
29:37.714 --> 29:38.965
[in Korean] Sorry?

527
29:39.883 --> 29:41.176
Uh, uh, uh…

528
29:41.259 --> 29:42.594
Hold on.

529
29:42.677 --> 29:44.054
Hold on.

530
29:45.347 --> 29:47.015
[in English] It's fine. Forget about it.

531
29:47.099 --> 29:48.517
How about some music?

532
29:50.644 --> 29:52.813
[♪ haunting music playing]

533
29:52.896 --> 29:54.606
[driver humming along]

534
30:05.283 --> 30:06.785
[in Korean] This feels a little off.

535
30:06.868 --> 30:08.995
MAP SEARCH

536
30:10.747 --> 30:12.666
[♪ haunting music continues]

537
30:36.356 --> 30:37.482
Karin?

538
30:38.233 --> 30:40.735
-[in English] Hey, why are you still here? -Mari!

539
30:40.819 --> 30:42.904
Ah, you're here. I'm so glad.

540
30:42.988 --> 30:45.532
You forgot to bring your medication again, didn't you?

541
30:45.615 --> 30:49.786
That's why I tried to get home as soon as possible, but Daniel…

542
30:49.870 --> 30:51.872
What about my sweet little Daniel?

543
30:53.206 --> 30:54.541
Huh?

544
30:54.624 --> 30:57.752
Yesterday, Daniel and I, um, kind of…

545
30:58.753 --> 30:59.880
He took off.

546
31:01.381 --> 31:03.717
-What? -Daniel quit today.

547
31:03.800 --> 31:06.344
-He went back to Germany. -[gasps]

548
31:06.428 --> 31:10.307
[whimpers] Just when I finally let him kiss me.

549
31:10.390 --> 31:11.766
No way. Ugh.

550
31:11.850 --> 31:14.728
Is that what he was planning to do all along?

551
31:14.811 --> 31:18.815
Is that why he kissed me so passionately?

552
31:18.899 --> 31:20.817
Oh, how annoying.

553
31:20.901 --> 31:23.278
[whimpers]

554
31:23.361 --> 31:26.489
-Hey! Wait till you're back on the island. -Why?

555
31:26.573 --> 31:28.241
The tarot cards said that we had a strong bond.

556
31:28.325 --> 31:31.870
-Stop! I need a drink! Come on! -Knock it off.

557
31:31.953 --> 31:34.873
-Let go! -Wait until we're back!

558
31:39.669 --> 31:40.670
[Yubin] Whoa.

559
31:42.631 --> 31:45.967
[exclaiming]

560
31:46.051 --> 31:48.053
[♪ tense music playing]

561
31:55.644 --> 31:58.104
[in English] I gotta take care of something.

562
31:59.940 --> 32:01.733
[Yubin, in Korean] What? What is it?

563
32:11.868 --> 32:12.994
[gasps]

564
32:13.828 --> 32:15.121
[♪ tense music builds]

565
32:23.296 --> 32:24.756
[exclaims]

566
32:26.174 --> 32:27.259
No!

567
32:27.342 --> 32:28.760
[thunder crashes]

568
32:35.225 --> 32:37.310
-[in English] This is a bad omen. -Huh? What is?

569
32:38.019 --> 32:41.064
I mean, look at the cards. The queen represents you.

570
32:41.147 --> 32:43.358
At first, you seem frail.

571
32:43.441 --> 32:45.568
-But you're resilient deep down. -Mm-hmm.

572
32:45.652 --> 32:49.281
Seven of Cups represents a situation with way too many choices.

573
32:49.990 --> 32:52.951
It could be a fantasy, or it could become reality.

574
32:53.910 --> 32:54.911
Is that a bad thing?

575
32:55.495 --> 32:58.123
The outcome would be up to you, my friend.

576
32:58.206 --> 33:01.960
-Tarot cards are such a sham. -You need to believe in it, Karin.

577
33:02.794 --> 33:05.297
Why? They were wrong about Daniel, right?

578
33:05.380 --> 33:07.340
They didn't predict him leaving.

579
33:08.758 --> 33:11.011
It's easiest to miss what's right under your nose.

580
33:13.805 --> 33:16.808
[chuckles] Tell me what this shiny one means.

581
33:17.350 --> 33:19.144
[gasps] It's the Wheel…

582
33:20.645 --> 33:21.771
of Fortune.

583
33:23.690 --> 33:26.067
It means you're bound to have a fated encounter

584
33:26.151 --> 33:28.570
camouflaged as a coincidence in the near future.

585
33:35.285 --> 33:36.828
It means fate?

586
33:43.626 --> 33:45.795
[in Korean] Where am I?

587
33:47.797 --> 33:50.342
[groans] I'm screwed. My phone's dying too.

588
33:52.218 --> 33:53.345
[exclaims]

589
33:54.262 --> 33:56.097
[sighs] I'm screwed.

590
33:57.766 --> 33:58.767
I'm screwed.

591
33:59.309 --> 34:00.310
[whimpers]

592
34:01.394 --> 34:03.146
I left all my stuff back there.

593
34:09.694 --> 34:10.695
[shouts]

594
34:11.321 --> 34:12.322
Dang it!

595
34:13.615 --> 34:14.908
[shouts]

596
34:17.202 --> 34:18.703
[in English] Excuse me!

597
34:18.787 --> 34:20.038
[in Korean] Hey!

598
34:21.581 --> 34:23.166
[exclaims]

599
34:23.249 --> 34:24.959
Come on, seriously.

600
34:26.044 --> 34:28.380
[groans] This place is just not for me.

601
34:34.469 --> 34:36.221
[♪ operatic music playing]

602
34:38.098 --> 34:39.891
[gasps]

603
34:43.686 --> 34:45.480
[in English] Why did you run away?

604
34:46.648 --> 34:47.649
Huh?

605
35:02.163 --> 35:04.290
CHARO VILLAGE OFFICE

606
35:04.374 --> 35:06.334
[Yubin] Thank you so much.

607
35:06.418 --> 35:09.295
-Thank you so much. -Huh. Strange.

608
35:10.338 --> 35:13.341
Karin already lives on the plot of land that you own.

609
35:14.467 --> 35:16.803
It's better to go and have yourselves a little chat.

610
35:17.429 --> 35:20.640
-Uh-- -Uh, you don't understand.

611
35:22.851 --> 35:25.687
Hey, Kunam, you know where Karin lives.

612
35:25.770 --> 35:27.647
-Can you give this guy a ride? -[gasps]

613
35:31.109 --> 35:32.944
[♪ whistling tunelessly]

614
35:38.199 --> 35:39.492
Oh…

615
35:47.125 --> 35:48.460
Here we are.

616
35:55.383 --> 35:56.676
Thank you very much.

617
35:58.261 --> 35:59.846
Thank you very much.

618
36:01.264 --> 36:02.932
-Are you all right? -Huh?

619
36:04.392 --> 36:05.935
[chuckles]

620
36:08.855 --> 36:11.107
[Yubin, in Korean] I think I'm right about this.

621
36:15.028 --> 36:17.155
[shouting, in Korean] Oh, my God…

622
36:23.203 --> 36:25.622
[in broken Korean] "Oh, my God." [in English] Is that right?

623
36:25.705 --> 36:28.708
[chuckles] "Oh, my God, Oh, my God" in Korean?

624
36:36.925 --> 36:38.635
[in Korean] Right? Yeah?

625
36:39.219 --> 36:41.513
Come on, I knew it. You're Korean.

626
36:42.764 --> 36:43.765
[in English] I don't…

627
36:47.060 --> 36:49.145
-[in Korean] You're right. I am. -Geez.

628
36:49.229 --> 36:52.524
Can I get your number? I think I'm going to need your help.

629
36:52.607 --> 36:55.068
I don't really speak the language here, so… Yeah?

630
36:57.737 --> 36:59.113
[in English] What a pain.

631
36:59.697 --> 37:00.907
[in Korean] All right, thanks.

632
37:02.784 --> 37:04.994
-[phone buzzing] -Calling. [in English] Okay.

633
37:06.579 --> 37:09.082
Okay. Block.

634
37:13.211 --> 37:16.172
-[in Korean] I know what "blocked" means. -Feel free to call me, sir.

635
37:17.048 --> 37:18.383
[engine starts]

636
37:29.686 --> 37:30.687
[sighs]

637
37:31.479 --> 37:32.564
So is this it?

638
37:35.567 --> 37:36.818
What's that?

639
37:40.697 --> 37:42.282
STRAWBERRY PICKING KAMINOSAWA FARM

640
37:42.365 --> 37:43.783
ALL YOU CAN EAT

641
37:43.867 --> 37:45.243
-[in English] Hey… -Huh?

642
37:45.994 --> 37:47.370
I was thinking…

643
37:47.954 --> 37:50.874
What if the tarot cards were describing my strawberries?

644
37:50.957 --> 37:54.168
Strawberries? That would be sad, don't you think?

645
37:54.252 --> 37:58.131
Sad? Why? I spent three years tending to my precious strawberries,

646
37:58.214 --> 38:00.174
and now they're finally getting recognition.

647
38:00.258 --> 38:02.427
-[sighs] -I couldn't be prouder of them.

648
38:02.510 --> 38:05.638
You think your strawberries have personalities?

649
38:05.722 --> 38:08.182
-Yeah, in some ways, they-- -Mari, you're here.

650
38:09.183 --> 38:11.436
Ooh. What great timing.

651
38:14.856 --> 38:16.774
-I'll hold it. -Thank you.

652
38:17.775 --> 38:20.862
Didn't I tell you? Kunam is totally head over heels for you.

653
38:20.945 --> 38:24.073
[chuckles] Yeah, well, he's not my type at all.

654
38:24.908 --> 38:26.910
Do you want to get dinner together?

655
38:26.993 --> 38:29.120
-Karin, do you wanna come too? -I can join?

656
38:29.203 --> 38:31.414
-Mm-hmm. -I almost forgot!

657
38:31.497 --> 38:34.125
There's some guy waiting for you at your place.

658
38:34.834 --> 38:36.753
Who is it? Do you know? What guy?

659
38:36.836 --> 38:38.004
Maybe Daniel's replacement?

660
38:38.087 --> 38:41.382
-Not that quickly. No way. -What did he look like? Was he hot?

661
38:41.466 --> 38:44.177
Was he hot? Not hotter than me. Come on.

662
38:47.513 --> 38:48.932
Sorry, Mari. I've gotta check.

663
38:49.015 --> 38:50.642
-See you later. -What? Hey, wait!

664
38:54.020 --> 38:55.688
It's just us.

665
38:57.565 --> 38:59.192
Sure. Why not?

666
38:59.275 --> 39:00.401
Come on.

667
39:01.611 --> 39:02.612
Yay!

668
39:04.447 --> 39:05.990
[Yubin] "Karin Farm"?

669
39:10.203 --> 39:11.454
[in Korean] What is this?

670
39:16.459 --> 39:18.544
Wait, is someone living here or what?

671
39:19.253 --> 39:20.421
Is this a farm?

672
39:22.048 --> 39:24.050
Wait, what the hell's going on here?

673
39:36.396 --> 39:37.730
Is someone living here?

674
39:41.651 --> 39:43.945
[children laughing, clamoring]

675
39:44.028 --> 39:45.863
[teacher, in English] Slow down! Careful!

676
39:45.947 --> 39:47.532
Don't lose your buddy!

677
39:50.368 --> 39:53.705
Excuse me. Can you tell me where the strawberry picking is?

678
39:53.788 --> 39:56.249
Over there? Or here?

679
39:56.332 --> 39:57.917
Uh… [speaks Japanese]

680
39:58.001 --> 40:00.086
-[in Korean] What? -[in English] Right there!

681
40:00.169 --> 40:02.171
Yay! Strawberries!

682
40:02.255 --> 40:04.173
[teacher] Be careful down the stairs!

683
40:06.926 --> 40:08.678
[child] Look at this one!

684
40:09.262 --> 40:11.472
-[in Korean] Well, this is… -[child, in English] Over here!

685
40:12.557 --> 40:14.976
[in Korean] Is this one of those strawberry-picking places?

686
40:18.646 --> 40:20.732
-[in English] Karin. -Oh, you're back!

687
40:20.815 --> 40:23.276
-I'm back. -So how was it? Will you pass this year?

688
40:23.359 --> 40:25.820
Mm-hmm. Green Nova is coming to inspect in three days,

689
40:25.903 --> 40:27.572
but I feel good about it.

690
40:29.615 --> 40:32.410
If 80% of my crop bears fruit, then I'll pass.

691
40:32.493 --> 40:34.704
[children screaming, clamoring]

692
40:34.787 --> 40:36.122
I've got this!

693
40:36.205 --> 40:37.331
-That's good. -That's great to hear.

694
40:37.415 --> 40:38.416
[Karin] Right?

695
40:43.379 --> 40:44.380
Ah!

696
40:44.464 --> 40:46.591
-Here. -[in Korean] Oh, these?

697
40:50.344 --> 40:51.929
[in English] Thank you very much.

698
40:54.432 --> 40:55.850
[in Korean] Okay.

699
41:04.776 --> 41:05.777
Mmm.

700
41:05.860 --> 41:08.029
[children shouting]

701
41:09.447 --> 41:11.824
-[in English] Hi there. -[child] Hello.

702
41:11.908 --> 41:14.160
-[chuckles] Hi. -Hello.

703
41:14.243 --> 41:15.536
Hello.

704
41:16.204 --> 41:17.330
[child] Yay!

705
41:31.761 --> 41:33.096
[gasps]

706
41:41.562 --> 41:43.564
What happened? What…

707
41:47.902 --> 41:50.571
What? This can't be…

708
41:52.198 --> 41:53.199
What?

709
41:57.954 --> 42:01.582
Over 80% of the field, uh, must bear fruit.

710
42:09.423 --> 42:11.592
[agency owner] On top of that,

711
42:11.676 --> 42:14.637
if your strawberries don't get certified this time,

712
42:15.346 --> 42:17.515
then your relief aid will get pulled.

713
42:17.598 --> 42:19.142
Are you sure you're not worried?

714
42:23.563 --> 42:25.648
[beeping]

715
42:35.032 --> 42:36.951
[in Korean] Are you the owner of…

716
42:38.536 --> 42:39.579
Huh?

717
42:41.873 --> 42:43.666
[in English] What are you doing?

718
42:44.959 --> 42:48.129
[watch beeping]

719
42:54.468 --> 42:57.096
[beeping accelerates]

720
43:03.269 --> 43:05.521
[♪ upbeat music playing]

721
43:32.882 --> 43:34.133
MERRY BERRY LOVE

722
43:34.217 --> 43:35.218
NEXT EPISODE

723
43:35.301 --> 43:39.180
You walked onto my private property and you single-handedly ruined everything.

724
43:40.014 --> 43:41.974
You're the new field worker?

725
43:42.058 --> 43:44.310
[Karin] He doesn't look like he's touched dirt in his entire life.

726
43:44.393 --> 43:48.314
[Yubin, in Korean] People fight. That's how you get close and build a bond.

727
43:49.232 --> 43:51.234
[♪ upbeat music plays]
